just-bash (vendored source copy)
Copyright 2024 Vercel Labs
License: Apache License 2.0
Source: https://github.com/vercel-labs/just-bash
Vendored at: DuskJS/src/vendor/just-bash
Used by:     DuskJS/src/binaries/jsh (the /bin/jsh binary)

DuskJS ships a fork of the just-bash source under `src/vendor/just-bash/`.
The vendored copy provides ~70 shell command implementations (grep, sed,
awk, find, sort, uniq, cut, cp, mv, jq, printf, tee, base64, xargs, and
many more) plus a POSIX-compatible shell parser and interpreter.
DuskJS wraps this in a `/bin/jsh` binary that runs each invocation with an
in-memory filesystem preloaded from DuskJS's own filesystem.

DuskJS-specific modifications to the vendored copy:
  - Removed: python3, sqlite3, curl (need host bridges not yet wired)
  - Removed: gzip/gunzip/zcat, tar, xan, html-to-markdown (heavy deps)
  - Replaced: js-exec now shells out to DuskJS's /bin/node (see
    src/vendor/just-bash/commands/js-exec/js-exec.ts)
  - Removed: overlay-fs and read-write-fs backends (use node:fs)
  - All source files carry `// @ts-nocheck` because DuskJS's tsconfig
    has stricter settings than upstream

